{"name":"Castlevania Heart","hex":"#a80020","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"heart","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A muscular organ that pumps blood through the body, traditionally thought to be the seat of emotion.","One's feelings and emotions, especially considered as part of one's character."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be fond of. Often bracketed or abbreviated with a heart symbol. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","To mark a comment, post, reply, etc., with the heart symbol (❤)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heart"}],"entries":[{"title":"Castlevania","blocks":[{"text":"Castlevania, known in Japan as Akumajō Dracula, is a gothic horror action-adventure video game series and media franchise created by Konami. The series is largely set in the castle of Count Dracula, the arch-enemy of the Belmont clan of vampire hunters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Castlevania_logo.png/330px-Castlevania_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Castlevania","wikidata":"Q2515184"},{"title":"Heart","blocks":[{"text":"The heart is a muscular organ found in humans and other animals. This organ pumps blood through the blood vessels. The heart and blood vessels together make up the circulatory system. The pumped blood carries oxygen and nutrients to the tissue, while carrying metabolic waste such as carbon dioxide to the lungs. In humans, the heart is approximately the size of a closed fist and is located between the lungs, in the middle compartment of the chest, called the mediastinum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png/330px-Heart_anterior_exterior_view.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heart","wikidata":"Q1072"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/50/Castlevania_nes_03.png/250px-Castlevania_nes_03.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/50/Castlevania_nes_03.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/50/Castlevania_nes_03.png/250px-Castlevania_nes_03.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gameplay of Castlevania on the NES. The player-character Simon Belmont attacks an enemy with the whip, which can be increased in length by collecting upgrades.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACastlevania_nes_03.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/16/CPoR-BattleScreen.jpg/250px-CPoR-BattleScreen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/16/CPoR-BattleScreen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/1/16/CPoR-BattleScreen.jpg/250px-CPoR-BattleScreen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Screenshot of Castlevania: Portrait of Ruin, which features Metroidvania gameplay. In the top screen is the map, which records the player's progress as they explore the castle.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACPoR-BattleScreen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d4/GrimoireofSoulscast.png/330px-GrimoireofSoulscast.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d4/GrimoireofSoulscast.png/330px-GrimoireofSoulscast.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Artwork of characters from Castlevania: Grimoire of Souls (2019) by Ayami Kojima. Kojima was hired in 1997 to i